## 8. Unverified / residual limits (honest negatives)

- **Reason semantics remain unverified by construction.** A fluent but false
  reason passes every shape check; the defence is the stale-exemption check
  plus human review, and the header says exactly that. I did not try to
  build a meaning check — it is not decidable in-script.
- Non-include `--macro` side effects, `--next/--each` flattening, `@:test`
  modules outside `<guarded-cp>/tests`, and test ids stay out of scope — all
  now explicitly declared in the header's NOT-COVERED list (header and
  implementation aligned line-by-line for every "always fails / exhaustive"
  wording I touched or reviewed).
- F9 (existence accepted for roots not on any classpath) is only fixed for
  file roots (strict per-file resolution, no repo-wide fallback);
  allowlist/floor modules still resolve against the union + repo fallback,
  by design and documented in header (3).
- The haxe probes verify the trimmed-line grammar; I did not re-run the
  f2 pass's full include()-semantics matrix (package-dir reject measured by
  them; my `f3-include` case exercises the guard's code path but I did not
  run an independent haxe compile for that exact case).
- One deliberate strictness boundary: any `--macro` line that is not
  `include(...)` is left unparsed (out of scope, documented); a one-sided
  non-include macro that changes the compiled set remains undetectable — by
  design, per header.
